From 068329cbdb6a8b8bbf700904831d05f46e34b55b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pugant <pugant@localhost>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 11:39:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] common: tolerate duplicated tool-call params in tagged
 peg-native grammar
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A model may re-emit a required parameter at the end of a long generation
(04/09 task 29340: write emitted path, content, path). The tagged grammar
admitted each required arg exactly once, so the whole tool call failed to
parse and the server threw the generation away ("does not match the
expected peg-native format") — 4m19s of work lost, manual intervention.

- grammar: after the required sequence, any arg may now repeat (optional
  args already could)
- mapper: duplicates resolve last-wins (previous pair surgically removed,
  other keys and their order preserved) and emit a greppable warning
  "peg-native: leniency-hit: duplicate param '<name>' tolerated (last-wins)"
  so the format-slip signal stays observable (pi_agent ack 04/09 11:00)

Test: tagged_duplicate_required_param (identical dup, divergent dup
last-wins, marker logged via captured log). Suites green:
test-chat-auto-parser 71/420, test-chat-peg-parser 32/198.

Co-Authored-By: GLM by z.ai <noreply@z.ai>
